---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../styles/templates/tools.css';
---

<Layout
  title="Ring Size Chart — Bez Ambar"
  description="Find your perfect ring size with our US and international ring size chart, measurement guide, and professional fitting tips."
  canonical="https://bezambar.com/ring-size-chart"
>

  <div class="ba-light-hero">
    <h1>Ring Size Chart</h1>
    <p>Finding your perfect ring size is essential for a comfortable fit. Use our guide below to measure your ring size at home, or visit us in Los Angeles for a professional fitting.</p>
  </div>

  <p class="ba-contact-note">Have questions? Call us at <a href="tel:2136299191">213-629-9191</a> and our team will be happy to assist you.</p>

  <section class="ba-page-section">
    <h2>How to Measure Your Ring Size at Home</h2>
    <div class="ba-info-grid">
      <div class="ba-info-card">
        <h3>Method 1: Measure an Existing Ring</h3>
        <ol>
          <li>Find a ring that fits the intended finger comfortably.</li>
          <li>Measure the inside diameter in millimeters.</li>
          <li>Match the measurement to the chart below.</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
      <div class="ba-info-card">
        <h3>Method 2: Use a String or Paper Strip</h3>
        <ol>
          <li>Cut a thin strip of paper and wrap it around the base of the ring finger.</li>
          <li>Mark the point where the strip overlaps.</li>
          <li>Measure the length in millimeters with a ruler.</li>
          <li>Match the circumference to the chart below.</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="ba-info-card" style="margin-bottom:24px;">
      <h3>Tips for an Accurate Measurement</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Measure your finger over the knuckle to ensure the ring slides on comfortably.</li>
        <li>Fingers swell in summer. Measure during warm conditions for a realistic fit.</li>
        <li>Wider bands fit tighter. Add a quarter size when purchasing a wide band.</li>
        <li>Warm up your hands before measuring for the most accurate result.</li>
        <li>Your dominant hand tends to be slightly larger. Measure the specific finger you plan to wear the ring on.</li>
        <li>Do not measure when your finger is swollen from exercise, heat, or salt intake.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <p>For the most accurate sizing, we recommend visiting a local jeweler who can use a professional mandrel or finger gauge.</p>
  </section>

